  data: {
    LLM: "Prioritize exposing the Aces. If an Ace is buried at the bottom of a 6-card column, you must calculate exactly how many moves it will take to move the 5 cards on top of it without losing access to those cards.\n\nThe 'Two-Way Loop': Use the ability to build up and down to shuffle cards between columns. If you have a 4 of Hearts and a 6 of Hearts in different piles, and the 5 of Hearts is available, you can use the 5 to bridge the gap and move segments of the suit together.\n\nConserve Spaces: Do not empty a column unless you have a definitive path to victory. Empty spaces can be filled with any card, but losing a column still reduces maneuverability; use spaces wisely.",
    Player: "Prioritize exposing the Aces. If an Ace is buried at the bottom of a 6-card column, you must calculate exactly how many moves it will take to move the 5 cards on top of it without losing access to those cards.\n\nThe 'Two-Way Loop': Use the ability to build up and down to shuffle cards between columns. If you have a 4 of Hearts and a 6 of Hearts in different piles, and the 5 of Hearts is available, you can use the 5 to bridge the gap and move segments of the suit together.\n\nConserve Spaces: Do not empty a column unless you have a definitive path to victory. Empty spaces can be filled with any card, but losing a column still reduces maneuverability; use spaces wisely.",
    aggressiveness: 0.5,
    riskTolerance: 0.5,
