    basic: 'Prioritize exposing the Aces. If an Ace is buried at the bottom of a 6-card column, you must calculate exactly how many moves it will take to move the 5 cards on top of it without losing access to those cards.',
    intermediate: "The 'Two-Way Loop': Use the ability to build up and down to shuffle cards between columns. If you have a 4 of Hearts and a 6 of Hearts in different piles, and the 5 of Hearts is available, you can use the 5 to bridge the gap and move segments of the suit together.",
    advanced: 'Conserve Spaces: Do not empty a column unless you have a definitive path to victory. Empty spaces can be filled with any card, but losing a column still reduces maneuverability; use spaces wisely.',
    tips: [
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "Look for 'blocked suits'. If the King of Clubs is on top of the Ace of Clubs, that suit is effectively frozen until you can move the King to another pile.",
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: 'Always prioritize moves to the foundation over moves within the tableau, unless a tableau move helps unbury a hidden Ace.',
      },
